// The never-throw rule of AGENTS.md as a Biome linter plugin: a `throw` under src/ is a BUG: invariant (a
// programming error no user can cause) or a bare rethrow of the catch binding; anything else is a failure the
// caller should receive as a Result.
//
// Reach and exemptions are the plugin's `overrides` entry in biome.json, with `includes` relative to the repository
// root; a top-level `plugins[].includes` matches the absolute path (biomejs/biome#11082), so the checkout's parent
// directories would decide the reach. The rule covers src/** only; .github/scripts/ stays exempt by policy, since a
// build script may throw on a user-caused failure.
//   src/cli/inputs.ts  -> exempt: commander's argParser can only refuse a value by throwing InvalidArgumentError
//
// GritQL has no scopes, so a second binding of the caught name anywhere in the catch body flags every rethrow in that
// body, not only the shadowed one; the fix is to rename. The regex reads the literal's source text, so BUG: must open
// the string or template itself.
//   a declaration, a destructuring, a nested function's parameter  -> a binding
//   a namespace, an `import x = require()`                          -> a binding
//   a function-type parameter in a cast, return type, or signature  -> a binding
//   a name in a type alias, an interface, or a type annotation       -> not one: nothing there holds a value

`throw $arg` as $throw where {
  not or {
    and {
      $arg <: JsNewExpression(arguments=JsCallArguments(args=[$first, ...])),
      or { $first <: JsStringLiteralExpression(), $first <: JsTemplateExpression() },
      $first <: r"^[\"'`]BUG:[\s\S]*"
    },
    and {
      $arg <: JsIdentifierExpression(),
      // A throw from a function nested in the catch body may run after the clause has ended, and one from a try
      // nested there is caught or rethrown by that try, so the walk up from the throw to its clause stops at both.
      $throw <: within JsCatchClause(declaration=JsCatchDeclaration(binding=$arg), body=$body) until or {
        JsTryStatement(),
        JsTryFinallyStatement(),
        JsArrowFunctionExpression(),
        JsFunctionExpression(),
        JsFunctionDeclaration(),
        JsMethodObjectMember(),
        JsMethodClassMember(),
        JsGetterObjectMember(),
        JsSetterObjectMember(),
        JsGetterClassMember(),
        JsSetterClassMember(),
        JsConstructorClassMember()
      },
      not $body <: contains or {
        JsIdentifierBinding() as $binding where {
          not $binding <: within or {
            TsTypeAnnotation(),
            TsTypeAliasDeclaration(),
            TsInterfaceDeclaration()
          }
        },
        TsModuleDeclaration(name=$binding),
        TsImportEqualsDeclaration(id=$binding)
      } where { $binding <: $arg }
    }
  },
  register_diagnostic(span=$throw, message="throw outside the never-throw rule: not a BUG: invariant (an Error whose message starts with BUG:) and not a bare rethrow of the catch binding; return a Result instead")
}
